Graphics settings (RA2_GFX), picture only.

How the engine draws: a flat 2D isometric renderer on SDL_Renderer (GPU when SDL has one, software
otherwise): SHP and terrain art blitted as textures, voxel units rasterised on the CPU into sprites,
shroud as per-cell tiles, no geometry, no shaders. So MSAA and anisotropic filtering have nothing to
act on and are not offered; sprite edges are smoothed by the 2x EPX upscaler of 0103.
- Scale= nearest / integer / bilinear / sharp / auto and Smooth= for the canvas-to-window step.
- Sprites= aa (default, 0103) / scale2x (classic EPX) / off.
- Bloom=, Vignette=, Grade= on the world view only, from SDL blends (post_fx.cpp), no shaders.
- ZoomSmooth= glides the wheel zoom to its target around the pointer; ZoomRange=wide widens the range.
Defaults are the old picture exactly. Tests: test_gfx_settings.cpp, test_pixel_scale.cpp.

